  "instance_name": "abusive_police_memes",
  "label": "Abusive Police Memes",
  "description": "A category of internet memes that use the image of police officers in a seemingly benign or friendly context to juxtapose with violent or threatening text, often to provoke fear, justify violence, or critique policing. These memes are considered abusive because they imply or threaten lethal force against civilians without specifying a target group, and use the authority figure's image to dehumanize or incite fear. The phrase 'this is why we shoot you guys' is a common trope in such memes, implying that the officer's demeanor or presence justifies lethal force.",
